    "table csv": "Entry,Si/Ge,(Si+Ge)/Al,Products,Crystallinity (%)\n1,10,50,ITQ-13,100\n2,15,50,ITQ-13,98.6\n3,20,50,ITQ-13,95.6\n4,30,50,ITQ-13,92.3\n5,40,50,ITQ-13,92.9\n6,50,50,Amorphous,–\n7,∞,50,EU-1,–\n8,10,30,ITQ-13,91.7\n9,30,30,Amorphous,–\n10,30,40,ITQ-13,90.4\n11,30,100,ITQ-13,98.3\n12,30,200,ITQ-13,98.7\n13,30,300,ITQ-13,94.9\n14,30,500,ITQ-13,91.8",
    "extracted text": "Al-Ge-ITQ-13 was hydrothermally synthesized by modifying the procedures reported by Castañeda and co-workers. Namely, appropriate amounts of TEOS (Sinopharm Chem. Reagent Co., Ltd.) were first added dropwise into an aqueous solution of hexamethonium dihydroxide (R(OH)2) and continuously stirred at 40–50°C for more than 4 h to ensure complete hydrolysis of TEOS and evaporation of generated ethanol. Then germanium oxide (GeO2) (99.98%, Alfa) and aluminum isopropoxide (Sinopharm Chem. Reagent Co., Ltd.) were added. After a viscous and homogeneous white gel was formed, a certain amount of hydrofluoric acid (40%, Sinopharm Chem. Reagent Co., Ltd.) was added. The molar compositions of the resultant gel were as follows: (1−x)SiO2:xGeO2:0.25R(OH)2:0.5HF:5H2O:yAl2O3, where x = 0.024–0.091 and y = 0–0.017. Finally, the obtained gel was transferred into a Teflon-lined stainless steel autoclave and crystallized at 135–150°C for 7–15 d under rotation.",
    "property mapping": "Si/Ge - The ratio of silicon to germanium in the synthesis gel\n(Si+Ge)/Al - The ratio of combined silicon and germanium to aluminum in the synthesis gel\nSiO2 - Silicon source (Si)\nGeO2 - Germanium source (Ge)\nR(OH)2 - Hexamethonium dihydroxide (OSDA)\nHF - Hydrofluoric acid\nH2O - Water\nAl2O3 - Aluminum source (Al)\nx - Mole fraction of GeO2 in the synthesis gel (0.024-0.091)\ny - Mole fraction of Al2O3 in the synthesis gel (0-0.017)",
    "formula abbreviations": "R(OH)2 = Hexamethonium dihydroxide (structure directing agent)\nx = Mole fraction of GeO2 in the synthesis gel (0.024-0.091)\ny = Mole fraction of Al2O3 in the synthesis gel (0-0.017)\nCrystallization time is provided in days (d) which needs to be converted to hours (7-15 days = 168-360 hours)",
    "ratio calculations": "For the general formula (1−x)SiO2:xGeO2:0.25R(OH)2:0.5HF:5H2O:yAl2O3, we need to normalize to Si = 1.0\n\nSi = (1-x) which varies depending on x value\nTo normalize to Si = 1.0, we divide all components by (1-x)\n\nNormalized formula: 1.0 SiO2 : [x/(1-x)] GeO2 : [0.25/(1-x)] R(OH)2 : [0.5/(1-x)] HF : [5/(1-x)] H2O : [y/(1-x)] Al2O3\n\nNote that Al2O3 contains 2 Al atoms per formula unit, so Al = 2y\n\nFor specific recipes in the table, Si/Ge ratios are given directly. For example:\nWhen Si/Ge = 10, Ge = Si/10 = 0.1 (normalized to Si = 1.0)\nWhen (Si+Ge)/Al = 50, Al = (Si+Ge)/50 = (1+Ge)/50",
